  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1,500eb<br>\n<strong>Humanity Loss:</strong> 14 (4d6)</p>\n<p>Neuralware. Borgware. Requires 2 Neuralware Option Slots.<br>\nDuration: 3 rounds (9 seconds)<br>\nPrimary Effects:<br>\n+3 to Initiative.<br>\n+1 to Evasion against one target per round.<br>\nSecondary Effects (Limit 1 Per Round):<br>\n+1 to one Attack made with the Archery, Autofire, Handguns, Heavy Weapons, or Shoulder Arms Skill.<br>\nIncrease MOVE by 1 until the end of the round, to a maximum of 10.</p>\n<p>Note: Activating the Zetatech Sandevistan causes the user to suffer 1d6 Humanity Loss. The Zetatech Sandevistan may only be activated once per hour. Using the Secondary Effect will cause the user to suffer 3 Humanity Loss each time they are used.</p>\n<p><strong>Type:</strong> Neuralware<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> uses 2</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Activate it like the core Sandevistan: the Primary Effects are toggles in the roll dialog, on by default, and the Secondary Effects are toggles that start off. Turn on only the ones you use.</li>\n<li>The Secondary Effect's MOVE +1 is not automated.</li>\n<li>Its Note names the Zetatech Sandevistan; the sheet probably means the Dynalar.</li>\n<li>Humanity Loss for activating it and for each Secondary Effect is not automated.</li>\n<li>The sheet gives no install location, so it uses the core Sandevistan's (Clinic).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From Bontari Homebrew Cyberpunk Items by Bontari (Sandevistans).</em></p>"
  },
